Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Time Evolution", "Title",
 CellID->509267359,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumEvolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],
 " solves the equation of motion of a quantum system. Which equation that is \
depends on what you hand it: the Schrodinger equation for a closed system, \
the Lindblad master equation once jump operators are present, the Heisenberg \
equation when the thing being evolved is an operator, and the Kossakowski \
equation when the jump operators are correlated."
}], "Text",
 CellID->329621944,ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],

Cell["\<\
The call is the same shape in every case - a Hamiltonian, optionally some \
dissipation, an initial condition, and a time - and the result is always an \
object that depends on time. Supply a time to it and you get an ordinary \
state or operator back, which answers every property the framework knows \
about.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->515379898,ExpressionUUID->"75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two choices control everything else. A bare symbol for the time solves the \
equation ",
 StyleBox["exactly", "TI"],
 ", through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["DSolve"]], "paclet:ref/DSolve"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],
 "; a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "t0", ",", " ", "t1"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],
 " interval solves it ",
 StyleBox["numerically", "TI"],
 ", through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["NDSolve"]], "paclet:ref/NDSolve"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],
 ". And an initial condition of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["None"]], "paclet:ref/None"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],
 " evolves the propagator instead of any particular state, which can then be \
applied to whatever state you like."
}], "Text",
 CellID->604760901,ExpressionUUID->"56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"<<", " ", "Wolfram`QuantumFramework`"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",
 CellID->1476799103,ExpressionUUID->"5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],

Cell["A Driven Qubit", "Section",
 CellID->448336599,ExpressionUUID->"3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 Cell[BoxData["PauliX"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],
 " Hamiltonian drives a qubit between ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],
 ". Evolving ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],
 " over one full period:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->970785311,ExpressionUUID->"6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"psi", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<PauliX\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<0\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",
 CellID->1377816002,ExpressionUUID->"23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is a state as a function of time, and ",
 Cell[BoxData["t"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],
 " is recorded on it as a parameter:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1439899046,ExpressionUUID->"569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"psi", "[", "\"\<Parameters\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",
 CellID->1641200340,ExpressionUUID->"15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Supplying a time gives the state at that time - an ordinary ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["QuantumState"]], 
    "paclet:Wolfram/QuantumFramework/ref/QuantumState", 
    "Wolfram/QuantumFramework Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],
 " with nothing left symbolic:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1424533854,ExpressionUUID->"2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"psi", "[", "1.", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->535457321,ExpressionUUID->"76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],

Cell["From there every state property is available as usual:", "Text",
 CellID->141959522,ExpressionUUID->"0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"psi", "[", "1.", "]"}], "[", "\"\<ProbabilitiesList\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",
 CellID->299517738,ExpressionUUID->"4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],

Cell["\<\
Sampling the interval shows the population sloshing between the two levels \
and back:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2142391071,ExpressionUUID->"741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"psi", "[", "t", "]"}], "[", "\"\<ProbabilitiesList\>\"", "]"}],
      ",", " ", "0.0001"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",
 CellID->1002769646,ExpressionUUID->"3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],

Cell["Plotting it gives the Rabi oscillation:", "Text",
 CellID->436346740,ExpressionUUID->"07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"psi", "[", "t", "]"}], "[", "\"\<ProbabilitiesList\>\"", "]"}], 
    "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"AxesLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<t\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<population of |1\[RightAngleBracket]\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",
 CellID->2122865143,ExpressionUUID->"3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],

Cell["What the Solution Actually Is", "Section",
 CellID->1735808809,ExpressionUUID->"1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A numerically evolved state is not a table of samples and it is not a \
symbolic expression. Its amplitudes ",
 StyleBox["are", "TI"],
 " the solver's own ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InterpolatingFunction"]], "paclet:ref/InterpolatingFunction"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],
 ", held as the state's array and applied to the time parameter:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->753514147,ExpressionUUID->"04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"psi", "[", "\"\<State\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",
 CellID->1164297175,ExpressionUUID->"1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],

Cell["\<\
That single object carries the whole two-component solution, so the state \
still knows its own shape without interpolating anything:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->632614636,ExpressionUUID->"6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"psi", "[", "\"\<Dimensions\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",
 CellID->1689610856,ExpressionUUID->"4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Nothing is computed until a time is supplied; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"psi", "[", "1.", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],
 " is what triggers an interpolation. This matters for large systems, where \
the alternative - one scalar interpolation per amplitude, each carrying its \
own copy of the solver's time grid - costs a copy of that grid per dimension. \
Asking for it explicitly with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<Expand\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],
 " shows what is being avoided:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1303163127,ExpressionUUID->"110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"expanded", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<PauliX\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<0\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Expand\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
  RowBox[{"expanded", "[", "\"\<State\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:= ",
 CellID->2098230307,ExpressionUUID->"76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],

Cell["The two forms give the same numbers:", "Text",
 CellID->1930159659,ExpressionUUID->"2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"expanded", "[", "1.", "]"}], "[", "\"\<ProbabilitiesList\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:= ",
 CellID->1113655915,ExpressionUUID->"35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],

Cell["Exact Solutions", "Section",
 CellID->1606118752,ExpressionUUID->"4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],

Cell["\<\
Passing a bare symbol instead of an interval solves the equation symbolically \
rather than numerically:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2141499446,ExpressionUUID->"65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"exact", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<PauliX\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<0\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "t"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
   RowBox[{"exact", "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[12]:= ",
 CellID->339082558,ExpressionUUID->"7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],

Cell["\<\
That is the textbook solution, and its populations are what the plot above \
traced:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->432388834,ExpressionUUID->"4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"exact", "[", "\"\<ProbabilitiesList\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"t", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:= ",
 CellID->443736588,ExpressionUUID->"02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],

Cell["\<\
The initial state may be symbolic too, in which case so is the answer:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1593449978,ExpressionUUID->"034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<X\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", " ", "\[Beta]"}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      "t"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[14]:= ",
 CellID->1742646261,ExpressionUUID->"52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Omit the initial state and the time entirely and the register state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],
 " is used, with the formal symbol ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],
 " as the time parameter. This is the shortest thing that says anything:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->29467524,ExpressionUUID->"2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<X\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:= ",
 CellID->1939141443,ExpressionUUID->"6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],

Cell["\<\
The numerical solution agrees with the closed form to the solver's tolerance:\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->5047578,ExpressionUUID->"608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"psi", "[", "1.", "]"}], "[", "\"\<ProbabilitiesList\>\"", "]"}],
     " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "1.", "]"}], " ", "^", " ", "2"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "1.", "]"}], " ", "^", " ", "2"}]}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:= ",
 CellID->15008895,ExpressionUUID->"2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],

Cell["Time-Dependent Hamiltonians", "Section",
 CellID->1892712309,ExpressionUUID->"66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Nothing requires the Hamiltonian to be constant. A symbol in it that \
matches the evolution parameter simply makes the generator time dependent. \
This is a spin with splitting ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],
 " driven transversally at the same frequency - a resonant drive:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->787969749,ExpressionUUID->"5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Omega]0", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Omega]p", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "10"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tf", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"2", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "\[Omega]p"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"driven", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Omega]0", " ", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<JZ\>\"", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Omega]p", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Omega]0", " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<JX\>\"", "]"}]}]}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[17]:= ",
 CellID->525088789,ExpressionUUID->"644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],

Cell["\<\
With no initial state given, the register state is used, so the Hamiltonian \
and the time interval are the whole call:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->357930410,ExpressionUUID->"2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"rabi", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
   RowBox[{"driven", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "tf"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[18]:= ",
 CellID->1802489801,ExpressionUUID->"6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Bloch vector traces the slow Rabi nutation underneath the fast Larmor \
precession. Over the interval ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", "/", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],
 " it makes one full circuit from the north pole and back:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->115301326,ExpressionUUID->"7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Evaluate", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"rabi", "[", "t", "]"}], "[", "\"\<BlochVector\>\"", "]"}], 
     "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "tf"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Subscript", "[", 
       RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", "x"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Subscript", "[", 
       RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", "y"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Subscript", "[", 
       RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", "z"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[19]:= ",
 CellID->1651187567,ExpressionUUID->"7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Halfway through, the spin has been driven to the south pole - a ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Pi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],
 " pulse:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->941376513,ExpressionUUID->"5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"rabi", "[", 
       RowBox[{"tf", "/", "2"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<BlochVector\>\"", "]"}], 
     "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "0.0001"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[20]:= ",
 CellID->2120243592,ExpressionUUID->"3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],

Cell["\<\
The evolution is unitary throughout, so the state stays pure and the Bloch \
vector stays on the sphere:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1047559317,ExpressionUUID->"6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"rabi", "[", 
   RowBox[{"tf", "/", "2"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<Purity\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[21]:= ",
 CellID->1820947576,ExpressionUUID->"55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],

Cell["Observables and Trajectories", "Section",
 CellID->670734585,ExpressionUUID->"4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],

Cell["\<\
An evolved state answers every ordinary state property once a time is given, \
so an observable is measured as it would be on any state:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->58232708,ExpressionUUID->"1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"QuantumMeasurement", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumMeasurementOperator", "[", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<PauliZ\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "@",
     " ", 
    RowBox[{"psi", "[", "1.", "]"}]}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<Mean\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[22]:= ",
 CellID->393464600,ExpressionUUID->"2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For a qubit the Bloch vector gives the motion directly. Under ",
 Cell[BoxData["PauliX"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],
 " the state precesses about the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],
 " axis, so the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],
 " component stays zero:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1484396876,ExpressionUUID->"25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"psi", "[", "1.", "]"}], "[", "\"\<BlochCartesianCoordinates\>\"", 
   "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[23]:= ",
 CellID->1149283354,ExpressionUUID->"04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],

Cell["\<\
Drawing that as a curve on the Bloch sphere shows the precession as the great \
circle it is:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1092188694,ExpressionUUID->"2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Show", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<UniformMixture\>\"", "]"}], 
    "[", "\"\<BlochPlot\>\"", "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"ParametricPlot3D", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Evaluate", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"psi", "[", "t", "]"}], "[", "\"\<BlochVector\>\"", "]"}], 
       "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[24]:= ",
 CellID->559599970,ExpressionUUID->"2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],

Cell["Open Systems: the Lindblad Equation", "Section",
 CellID->1710123944,ExpressionUUID->"14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],

Cell["\<\
Jump operators turn the Schrodinger equation into the Lindblad master \
equation,\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->934597701,ExpressionUUID->"66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "-", 
      FractionBox["1", "2"], "{", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "}"}]}], ")"}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->284780108,ExpressionUUID->"48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],
 " the density matrix, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],
 " the jump operators and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],
 " their rates. Passing them as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Ls", " ", "->", " ", "rates"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],
 " is enough to switch equations. Here a ",
 Cell[BoxData["PauliZ"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],
 " Hamiltonian with ",
 Cell[BoxData["PauliX"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],
 " dephasing at rate 0.6:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->643798763,ExpressionUUID->"5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"noisy", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<PauliZ\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<PauliX\>\"", "]"}], "}"}], " ", "->",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "0.6", "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
    RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<0\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[25]:= ",
 CellID->268959046,ExpressionUUID->"250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],

Cell["\<\
The state is a density matrix now rather than a vector, because dissipation \
does not preserve purity. Purity falls from 1 toward the maximally mixed \
value of 1/2:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->403125484,ExpressionUUID->"15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"noisy", "[", "t", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Purity\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[26]:= ",
 CellID->931950651,ExpressionUUID->"58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],

Cell["The populations equalize as it goes:", "Text",
 CellID->412518898,ExpressionUUID->"43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"noisy", "[", "3.", "]"}], "[", "\"\<ProbabilitiesList\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[27]:= ",
 CellID->622967176,ExpressionUUID->"341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],

Cell["Relaxing to a Thermal State", "Section",
 CellID->1358080856,ExpressionUUID->"1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Dephasing drives a qubit to the maximally mixed state because it has no \
preferred direction. Amplitude damping does have one, and at finite \
temperature the two directions compete. With a mean occupation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],
 " of the bath, decay happens at rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],
 " and absorption at rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", "n"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->320615307,ExpressionUUID->"07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", " ", "=", " ", "50"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", "3"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"H", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "/", "2"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<Z\>\"", "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Sigma]m", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Ls", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\[Sigma]m", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Sigma]m", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Gamma]s", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"n", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", "n"}], "}"}]}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[28]:= ",
 CellID->1594238871,ExpressionUUID->"7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],

Cell["Starting from a pure state tilted off the axis:", "Text",
 CellID->2002505366,ExpressionUUID->"68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[Rho]0", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "8"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{"I", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "4"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "8"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[29]:= ",
 CellID->2121396920,ExpressionUUID->"6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[Rho]t", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
   RowBox[{"H", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Ls", " ", "->", " ", "\[Gamma]s"}], ",", " ", "\[Rho]0", ",", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[30]:= ",
 CellID->993357154,ExpressionUUID->"4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "By ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],
 " the populations have all but reached the thermal ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", "\[ThinSpace]", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "/", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{"2", 
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],
 ", which for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "=", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "4", "/", "7"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"3", "/", "7", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->50259360,ExpressionUUID->"323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Rho]t", "[", "1.", "]"}], "[", "\"\<ProbabilitiesList\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[31]:= ",
 CellID->680111415,ExpressionUUID->"7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"N", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"n", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", "n"}], "}"}], "/", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[32]:= ",
 CellID->1912025938,ExpressionUUID->"511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The trajectory spirals in from the surface of the Bloch sphere toward that \
point, the fast ",
 Cell[BoxData["PauliZ"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],
 " precession winding around the slow decay:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1678275947,ExpressionUUID->"6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Show", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<UniformMixture\>\"", "]"}], 
    "[", "\"\<BlochPlot\>\"", "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"ParametricPlot3D", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Evaluate", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\[Rho]t", "[", "t", "]"}], "[", "\"\<BlochVector\>\"", "]"}],
        "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[33]:= ",
 CellID->1570109414,ExpressionUUID->"519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The rates can equally be folded into the operators as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"]]], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],
 ", in which case the jump operators are given as a plain list and the result \
is identical:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->746824257,ExpressionUUID->"06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Rho]t2", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
    RowBox[{"H", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]s", "]"}], " ", "Ls"}], ",", " ", 
     "\[Rho]0", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Rho]t2", "[", "1.", "]"}], "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", 
      "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Rho]t", "[", "1.", "]"}], "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", 
      "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[34]:= ",
 CellID->966663717,ExpressionUUID->"12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],

Cell["The Liouvillian and the Propagator", "Section",
 CellID->634665076,ExpressionUUID->"733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An open-system generator can be assembled on its own as a Liouvillian \
superoperator ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[ScriptCapitalL]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],
 ", the object with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["d",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", "\[ScriptCapitalL]", 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1607396713,ExpressionUUID->"65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalL]", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Liouvillian\>\"", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<Z\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "\[Sigma]m", "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "0.3", "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[35]:= ",
 CellID->171231949,ExpressionUUID->"5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],

Cell["\<\
It acts on a density matrix flattened into a vector, so for a qubit its \
matrix is 4x4 rather than 2x2:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->820919957,ExpressionUUID->"78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Dimensions", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalL]", "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[36]:= ",
 CellID->1006830744,ExpressionUUID->"08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Passing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["None"]], "paclet:ref/None"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],
 " in place of an initial state evolves the ",
 StyleBox["propagator", "TI"],
 " rather than any particular state. Given a Liouvillian this produces ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalL]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],
 ", the map that takes any initial density matrix to its state at time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1175763064,ExpressionUUID->"5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"U", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"I", " ", "\[ScriptCapitalL]"}], ",", " ", "None", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[37]:= ",
 CellID->1074416020,ExpressionUUID->"112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],

Cell["\<\
Because it is the map and not a trajectory, it can be applied to any state \
without solving again:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2143439988,ExpressionUUID->"6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Rho]start", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "8"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "8"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"U", "[", "2.", "]"}], "[", "\[Rho]start", "]"}], 
  "[", "\"\<ProbabilitiesList\>\"", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[38]:= ",
 CellID->1933756212,ExpressionUUID->"30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],

Cell["\<\
Solving the same problem directly as a Lindblad equation gives the same \
answer, to the solver's tolerance:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->943735407,ExpressionUUID->"29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<Z\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", "\[Sigma]m", "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "0.3", "}"}]}], ",", " ", "\[Rho]start", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "[", "2.", 
   "]"}], "[", "\"\<ProbabilitiesList\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[39]:= ",
 CellID->865519937,ExpressionUUID->"7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],

Cell["\<\
The propagator also exists for closed systems, where it is the familiar \
unitary. Solved exactly it is a closed form:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->845186625,ExpressionUUID->"3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<PauliX\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
      "None", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[40]:= ",
 CellID->14312863,ExpressionUUID->"62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],

Cell["The Heisenberg Picture", "Section",
 CellID->315698450,ExpressionUUID->"7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same superoperator run backwards evolves ",
 StyleBox["observables", "TI"],
 " instead of states. Taking its adjoint and applying it to an operator - \
passed through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["QuantumState"]], 
    "paclet:Wolfram/QuantumFramework/ref/QuantumState", 
    "Wolfram/QuantumFramework Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],
 " as a matrix state, then read back as an operator - gives ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1751204118,ExpressionUUID->"0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"A0", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<Z\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"At", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"U", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"A0", "[", "\"\<MatrixQuantumState\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], 
    "[", "\"\<Operator\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[41]:= ",
 CellID->2116603297,ExpressionUUID->"7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two pictures are two ways of writing the same number, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], "0"], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "0"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"],
 ". In the Schrodinger picture the state moves:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->530919167,ExpressionUUID->"1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
     RowBox[{"A0", "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"U", "[", "2.", "]"}], "[", "\[Rho]start", "]"}], 
      "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[42]:= ",
 CellID->1242319925,ExpressionUUID->"370294fd-9e49-2d35-5d31-0da71bfc741f"],

Cell["\<\
In the Heisenberg picture the observable moves and the state does not:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1600082692,ExpressionUUID->"2845529c-454d-b13b-587b-4bc66cf90001"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"At", "[", "2.", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], 
    " ", ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\[Rho]start", "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], 
   "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[43]:= ",
 CellID->1091979148,ExpressionUUID->"7519012f-e657-215b-2326-988893e273a1"],

Cell["\<\
They agree to machine precision across the interval, since both read the same \
solved propagator:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1239660989,ExpressionUUID->"594776df-9e75-d16a-0f7d-6f991b01a3b0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
         RowBox[{"A0", "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"U", "[", "t", "]"}], "[", "\[Rho]start", "]"}], 
          "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "-", "\n",
       "    ", 
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"At", "[", "t", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], 
        " ", ".", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\[Rho]start", "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], 
       "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "5", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[44]:= ",
 CellID->234435634,ExpressionUUID->"6405505f-4b92-3bd6-0c3b-4a196e24893c"],

Cell["The Kossakowski Equation", "Section",
 CellID->417968184,ExpressionUUID->"6878c7f8-419e-9db5-1807-dea27028e79f"],

Cell["\<\
The Lindblad equation assumes the jump operators are uncorrelated. Dropping \
that assumption gives the Kossakowski equation,\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1274591649,ExpressionUUID->"48a3d607-c312-9dd3-7850-c860f6a4e739"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"i", "j"}], "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"i", "j"}], "TI"]], "(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "-", 
      FractionBox["1", "2"], "{", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "}"}]}], ")"}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1243964799,ExpressionUUID->"539491e8-328f-8d7b-01ab-08b2473bd441"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "where the rates become a positive-semidefinite matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"i", "j"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fcf59b5-a5ca-2155-25f5-50fecc7f73bf"],
 " whose off-diagonal entries encode correlations between channels. A \
diagonal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Beta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "023f49e2-a747-9723-33c5-60cfd2f3fa09"],
 " recovers the Lindblad equation. Building the Liouvillian with a matrix in \
place of a list of rates is all it takes."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1828403510,ExpressionUUID->"21aa1c49-e16c-f406-57a9-9612901edf6c"],

Cell["\<\
Two atoms decaying into a shared field is the standard example. The \
Hamiltonian is just their bare energies:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->623026911,ExpressionUUID->"289b85cd-827f-9a9c-58b8-1c97370be8e6"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Omega]1", " ", "=", " ", "0.9"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Omega]2", " ", "=", " ", "0.7"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Hk", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Omega]1", "/", "2"}], " ", "\"\<ZI\>\""}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Omega]2", "/", "2"}], " ", "\"\<IZ\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[45]:= ",
 CellID->308489360,ExpressionUUID->"12f3dbee-abc4-6375-4280-d2cbce714e5f"],

Cell["Each atom decays through its own lowering operator:", "Text",
 CellID->387004599,ExpressionUUID->"7ed5da6f-a344-b859-26ea-dc48d6f60aa3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"jumpOps", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumTensorProduct", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "#", "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "#2", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "@@@",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<-\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<I\>\""}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<I\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<-\>\""}], "}"}]}], 
    "}"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[46]:= ",
 CellID->1976158344,ExpressionUUID->"2cfa2c34-ef50-7d46-5499-c6718ae547ac"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The correlation between the two channels is the off-diagonal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "12"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "362a4e41-4988-041f-5e2a-602b683d6f65"],
 "; the matrix is positive semidefinite as long as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[GreaterEqual]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "12"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01ed6b92-5a5f-fa78-3792-82dc5febc942"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1232186413,ExpressionUUID->"107fa29c-d013-1000-4004-3bd9e1a6636a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Gamma]d", " ", "=", " ", "0.5"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Gamma]12", " ", "=", " ", "0.45"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Beta]", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\[Gamma]d", ",", " ", "\[Gamma]12"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\[Gamma]12", ",", " ", "\[Gamma]d"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalL]k", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Liouvillian\>\"", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Hk", ",", " ", "jumpOps", ",", " ", "\[Beta]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Dimensions", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalL]k", "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[47]:= ",
 CellID->655687319,ExpressionUUID->"6798df62-4cc7-e4e1-0da7-d74c6573cecb"],

Cell["\<\
Evolve three initial states with one excitation between them - a product \
state, the singlet, and the triplet. When the Hamiltonian is already a \
superoperator, the initial state comes directly after it:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1589358908,ExpressionUUID->"49f5450b-e8d1-97dd-7f8b-5d548965fd27"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"states", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<01\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<PsiMinus\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<PsiPlus\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"evolved", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"I", " ", "\[ScriptCapitalL]k"}], ",", " ", "#", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
     "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "states"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[48]:= ",
 CellID->1191517648,ExpressionUUID->"2570a8a5-7a6f-59e7-530f-410f7f1a2bcd"],

Cell["\<\
Count the excitations left at each time with the total-number operator:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->960670710,ExpressionUUID->"0b990c23-b656-01a6-39a6-a58cc3e3538c"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"totalExcitation", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Total", " ", "@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"With", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"mat", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Array", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
          RowBox[{"mat", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", "#", "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", "2"}], 
       "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"excitations", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"#", "[", "t", "]"}], "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}],
            "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
           RowBox[{"totalExcitation", "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], 
         "]"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "5", ",", " ", "0.05"}], 
        "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "evolved"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[49]:= ",
 CellID->1307080411,ExpressionUUID->"52243646-2fbd-210e-03db-a8204a487054"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "All three start with one excitation and all three decay, but at three \
different rates. The correlation splits the symmetric and antisymmetric \
combinations apart: the singlet is subradiant, decaying at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "12"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1acd7f4d-3da3-7753-4af3-7717b4565db9"],
 ", and the triplet is superradiant, decaying at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "12"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "062d91f0-6326-41c0-2fd2-08ba16d3132a"],
 " - here a factor of nineteen between them:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1960030258,ExpressionUUID->"1ac7f74a-ce09-be58-4afc-ef17ebbd04a2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{"excitations", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DataRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<|01\[RightAngleBracket]\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<singlet\>\"", ",",
       " ", "\"\<triplet\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"AxesLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<t\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<excitations\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[50]:= ",
 CellID->535682707,ExpressionUUID->"6f6ad260-8ee1-565a-1569-d44a2a943ca0"],

Cell["At the end of the interval they are far apart:", "Text",
 CellID->1167207179,ExpressionUUID->"612fd791-c81e-86f2-10d4-cedae9a8ecd8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"excitations", "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "0.0001"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[51]:= ",
 CellID->1612953718,ExpressionUUID->"26dca2d1-2715-746d-4ee3-3b9b52a05eb7"],

Cell["Watching for Events", "Section",
 CellID->790826209,ExpressionUUID->"296a77cd-8fa3-dd44-5f6a-6e972a57a7ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<AdditionalEquations\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b853673-18d0-d9fa-19ba-a83d996aabc0"],
 " injects extra equations or specifications into the solve, which is how \
hybrid and piecewise systems are expressed - and how events are detected. \
Here a strong pulsed drive with a constant detuning:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1163030741,ExpressionUUID->"25b5b884-ef74-61b3-534a-31e18a013399"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"rabiDrive", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"10.", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Pi", " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<X\>\"", "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "\"\<1\>\"", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Operator\>\"",
      "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"pulsed", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
    RowBox[{"rabiDrive", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"pulsed", "[", "t", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Probability\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[52]:= ",
 CellID->1753119213,ExpressionUUID->"574a2197-51ef-7938-7d49-b8d1679a4802"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To find the times at which the population crosses one half, solve again \
with a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["WhenEvent"]], "paclet:ref/WhenEvent"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6e85e9ed-427b-8528-16ba-00b7770fec72"],
 ". The dependent variable of the internal differential equation is the \
formal symbol ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73b76025-96bb-3fff-214d-798f234f85c5"],
 ", so the condition is written on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Indexed", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[FormalS]", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31f4c073-8ff6-126f-678b-da3d298360b5"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Sow"]], "paclet:ref/Sow"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "72ff7667-e560-b2c0-2285-68408c1a002a"],
 "/",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Reap"]], "paclet:ref/Reap"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "7c9be80e-0554-61c1-24b8-0268ace1332b"],
 " collect the crossings:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2037256,ExpressionUUID->"106b7ad8-6378-599b-4069-7382160d2be1"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"sol", ",", " ", "points"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Reap", " ", "@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
     RowBox[{"rabiDrive", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
      
      RowBox[{"\"\<AdditionalEquations\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"WhenEvent", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
            RowBox[{"Indexed", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"\[FormalS]", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], 
            "]"}], " ", "^", " ", "2"}], " ", "==", " ", "0.5"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sow", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Length", "[", 
  RowBox[{"First", "[", "points", "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[53]:= ",
 CellID->339747688,ExpressionUUID->"7e6f7c7a-fa8f-2da1-2615-7627ff3a778b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Take", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"First", "[", "points", "]"}], ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   "0.0001"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[54]:= ",
 CellID->1569376968,ExpressionUUID->"304452a4-201b-d64c-607c-4b0e51afbc96"],

Cell["\<\
The crossings really are crossings - evaluating the returned solution at them \
gives one half back:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1336445995,ExpressionUUID->"6beff1f8-c64a-83a6-1994-e8a5f3fcd18c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"sol", "[", "#", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Probability\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"First", "[", "points", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "-", " ", "0.5"}], 
   "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[55]:= ",
 CellID->797627498,ExpressionUUID->"4b5b9263-9199-4e16-7978-144d202c157c"],

Cell["\<\
Shading the plot between them marks out the intervals where the qubit is \
mostly excited:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->151045137,ExpressionUUID->"475d7054-346c-a3cc-6d63-6a1ebd1ef116"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"sol", "[", "t", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Probability\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Mesh", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"First", "[", "points", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"MeshShading", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"Green", ",", " ", "Orange"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[56]:= ",
 CellID->1063989564,ExpressionUUID->"2ef71510-aa09-eca9-568c-8d5dcfbdb6f3"],

Cell["The Equations Themselves", "Section",
 CellID->1987333543,ExpressionUUID->"3343f580-98d5-e31c-6170-ecea1961ce66"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<ReturnEquations\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20a7420b-376a-b23f-505d-6455421c0105"],
 " stops short of solving and hands back the system instead, in exactly the \
form the solver would have been called with - equations, dependent variable, \
and time specification:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->616753397,ExpressionUUID->"6af863a9-1098-c609-1a98-7af3a112ad53"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<XX\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<ReturnEquations\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[57]:= ",
 CellID->1146256261,ExpressionUUID->"055bc2ad-6b92-a3be-3378-dbf70e24f184"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The generator is right there in the equation, and it is exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["H", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b0fb60e-2211-365f-5934-286857a59ca5"],
 " for the Hamiltonian that went in - here ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "201a2509-bdd9-2fa1-5039-bd53346c758b"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1280025883,ExpressionUUID->"7085d256-6adc-aa08-20ba-d4100f6ef952"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"eqs", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<XX\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<ReturnEquations\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
   RowBox[{"eqs", "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}],
    "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[58]:= ",
 CellID->681114160,ExpressionUUID->"5f932952-49a5-d34f-05a0-c11c6851a195"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Reaching for this is worthwhile when the system needs to be handed to a \
solver directly - to couple it to equations of a different kind, to pick a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Method"]], "paclet:ref/Method"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "160f17c4-d31a-fe19-3e34-8ea1e6acc563"],
 " by hand, or simply to see what is being integrated."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1719384190,ExpressionUUID->"10beb8bd-bdb6-ee93-4045-31e73440b4f9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The triple is in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["NDSolveValue"]], "paclet:ref/NDSolveValue"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3fdc991b-fead-14b0-65e3-1144fb587e9a"],
 "'s argument order, but two things in it are for the framework's benefit \
rather than the solver's: the matrices are sparse, which ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["NDSolveValue"]], "paclet:ref/NDSolveValue"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3657d2c5-05c0-ac85-5e6c-cbafac7af6ef"],
 " will not accept as an initial condition, and the dependent variable is a \
formal symbol. Make both ordinary and it runs:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1020643561,ExpressionUUID->"0642d375-09f3-9942-2e71-cb3faf87eba8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"solved", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"NDSolveValue", " ", "@@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"eqs", " ", "/.", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"sa_SparseArray", " ", ":>", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Normal", "[", "sa", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[FormalS]", " ", "->", " ", "s"}]}], "}"}]}], 
    ")"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[59]:= ",
 CellID->1064479054,ExpressionUUID->"0651775d-2bad-791b-2e6f-6f074e584861"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "What comes back is the same solution ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumEvolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63b9e3d6-2298-231e-1146-fa9057128e64"],
 " would have handed over wrapped in a state - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"00"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67c13665-f813-2f11-0dfe-a84ef9a6727b"],
 " rotating into ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"11"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c440104-ea8a-4285-747b-99618f3f10ef"],
 " as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c9a615-af45-c085-0ef6-385ecaf192ef"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0513e607-0f4c-1e20-3320-f861aaf9650a"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1710804206,ExpressionUUID->"0371ff35-cd30-cda2-310e-f77ee4ca9788"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
  RowBox[{"solved", "[", "1.", "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[60]:= ",
 CellID->762016048,ExpressionUUID->"6833ae6a-6ac5-a2c8-19c0-40340f71f012"],

Cell["Details", "Section",
 CellID->953318213,ExpressionUUID->"5f7f2999-1aee-25a5-0504-c0c39e988f8f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The time argument is either a symbol, which solves the equation exactly \
with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["DSolve"]], "paclet:ref/DSolve"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "128c7526-c883-085d-42b4-6c83e9365aa7"],
 ", or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "t0", ",", " ", "t1"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3279c00f-c9e2-8758-6206-da68ef94eda2"],
 ", which solves it numerically with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["NDSolve"]], "paclet:ref/NDSolve"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "50b12ff8-e606-85f7-004e-c6a593b0efdd"],
 ". Options not recognized by ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumEvolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "640f47a5-4648-c62d-0c35-5e0f73e2ad77"],
 " are passed through to whichever solver runs, so ",
 Cell[BoxData["AccuracyGoal"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63a48922-0fac-666c-115b-208caa594cb6"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["Method"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "387a9e0d-0234-0e73-6819-1057b7c15559"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["MaxSteps"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f64ca0d-9927-5f44-651b-ec5718d225ae"],
 " and the rest all work."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1320676321,ExpressionUUID->"399d1ff3-4632-be92-6fa2-96bd73c404f8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The initial condition selects the equation. A state gives the Schrodinger \
or Lindblad equation; an operator gives the Heisenberg equation; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["None"]], "paclet:ref/None"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1170384d-2f38-2c50-470f-b2174acd76ba"],
 " gives the propagator. Omitting it uses the register state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{"0", "\[Ellipsis]", "0"}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ce33075-6d34-44a7-1490-aa3f04c12e8d"],
 ", and omitting the time along with it uses the formal symbol ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "54e2b6d5-0ba4-5b19-7c91-2f9fae512663"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1600517155,ExpressionUUID->"6334ac9c-43f1-85c0-12cb-45c67585ef2a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Jump operators are given either as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"L1", ",", " ", "L2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\[Gamma]1", ",", " ", "\[Gamma]2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}]}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "74397683-04f4-1d4d-1dc7-6fedac816797"],
 " or as a plain list with the rates folded in as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"]]], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "735e49d5-32a1-4a48-2166-609f47541892"],
 ". Correlated channels need the Kossakowski form, which is reached by \
building ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Liouvillian\>\"", "[", 
     RowBox[{"H", ",", " ", "Ls", ",", " ", "\[Beta]"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "335d55a2-cf9b-493d-6163-4c0fea2e1807"],
 " with a rate matrix and evolving ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"I", " ", "\[ScriptCapitalL]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bfbbd45-edb8-1b0b-6998-352e844d6651"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1655262560,ExpressionUUID->"045023ab-c37d-b770-2c6f-baf4f6091a5a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With a Hamiltonian that is already a superoperator, the state argument \
comes directly after it: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalL]", ",", " ", "state", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "73e8aeff-5b91-f8f4-2197-47b95e25cade"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->843709254,ExpressionUUID->"33e490f1-5bc8-e939-619b-09bb5e62b803"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The evolution parameter is recorded on the returned object, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"state", "[", "\"\<Parameters\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "794a4309-908b-2549-2f4a-5b53213f8f93"],
 " names it and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"state", "[", "t", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "167ebcf0-2b32-2a61-3e05-35ba4ec7794b"],
 " supplies it."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1241281984,ExpressionUUID->"15eb24b6-b946-3a65-43e8-bdf038f0894f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A numerically evolved state holds the solver's ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InterpolatingFunction"]], "paclet:ref/InterpolatingFunction"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "27d2a24c-1e84-19ee-4de1-44169b316b34"],
 " as its amplitudes, so it answers questions about its shape without \
evaluating anything, and interpolation happens once a time is supplied. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<Expand\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "285985c7-a1c8-13eb-5866-1ca0d07d6131"],
 " instead stores one scalar interpolation per amplitude, each carrying its \
own copy of the solver's time grid."
}], "Item",
 CellID->2083544408,ExpressionUUID->"57868ed1-450c-c474-7dbd-279b6cbeaf5e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<MergeInterpolatingFunctions\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c5e608e-35dc-f74f-3466-79e8bc6edd95"],
 " controls what happens when the Hamiltonian itself contains interpolating \
functions of time. The default merges them into a single sparse \
interpolation, which is substantially faster than letting each enter the \
dynamical equation separately."
}], "Item",
 CellID->960626294,ExpressionUUID->"1a1e4090-3303-05ed-4a26-59da46b66f37"],

Cell["Possible Issues", "Section",
 CellID->1275597307,ExpressionUUID->"10256af3-3972-af7a-41da-83bdb804f240"],

Cell["\<\
Ask for amplitudes before supplying a time and the answer is a function of \
the parameter rather than numbers, which is rarely what is wanted from a \
numerical solve. Supply the time first:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->180386896,ExpressionUUID->"457602f1-d86e-ac86-730d-9bbad918f6ec"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"psi", "[", "0.5", "]"}], "[", "\"\<ProbabilitiesList\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[61]:= ",
 CellID->1150052415,ExpressionUUID->"499f95c1-a958-6c18-7fa4-0caac8ed3762"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The numerical and exact routes agree to the solver's tolerance, not to \
machine precision, and the difference above is around the eighth decimal. \
Tighten it with the usual ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["NDSolve"]], "paclet:ref/NDSolve"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "0f1e874b-6d22-b8ab-3525-1f1504d40af1"],
 " options."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1256596424,ExpressionUUID->"0c02104f-9807-e6c4-3431-8a2919b3cc2e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Defining a time-dependent Hamiltonian as a function of its time argument \
does not work the way it looks like it should. The operator's matrix is a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["SparseArray"]], "paclet:ref/SparseArray"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6f909018-5ea1-6a32-15af-0a425b543918"],
 ", and a pattern variable is not substituted into it, so the symbol in the \
stored expression is never replaced:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->969862745,ExpressionUUID->"2f4595f3-090a-1216-557a-0cbda8bf617c"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"badH", "[", "x_", "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<X\>\"", "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"badH", "[", "0.3", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[62]:= ",
 CellID->1199935485,ExpressionUUID->"06385f5e-e9d4-4e6c-2fd8-571b886114b6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Write the Hamiltonian as a plain expression in the evolution parameter \
instead, and let ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumEvolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25d2fb85-296f-82e5-53e1-f2ef481bd0cf"],
 " handle the substitution:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->641748961,ExpressionUUID->"3b9a140e-d97a-4136-69b9-8e6bd80f101c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "t", "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<X\>\"", "]"}]}], ")"}], 
   "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[63]:= ",
 CellID->1055869762,ExpressionUUID->"4f9438da-b80f-a114-75ab-b18439bbf07e"],

Cell["\<\
If the exact solver cannot find a closed form, the output is the unevaluated \
solver call it gave up on, along with a message. Here a Rabi problem with a \
general detuning, which has no elementary solution:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1607759830,ExpressionUUID->"7281c19b-2602-dcd4-22be-d8c553b4a63e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"Subscript", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[Omega]", ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<Z\>\"", "]"}]}], " ", "+", "\n", 
    "    ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Gamma]r", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Subscript", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\[Omega]", ",", " ", "p"}], "]"}], " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<X\>\"", "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", "t"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[64]:= ",
 CellID->1074210535,ExpressionUUID->"3c8746fc-db76-c487-64bd-5fb9de00aeed"],

Cell["\<\
Numbers in the Hamiltonian make the same problem solvable numerically, so the \
fallback when a closed form does not exist is to give the parameters values \
and pass an interval instead.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1050391292,ExpressionUUID->"11f0f87a-e6f0-91cd-478f-f227928ae317"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Related Guides", "TutorialMoreAboutSection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.843042384656711*^9, 3.843042386024461*^9}},
 CellID->23220180,ExpressionUUID->"473164ce-b547-c1f4-6ecf-7da83cf393de"],

Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
 TemplateBox[{
   Cell[
    TextData["WolframQuantumComputationFramework"]], 
   "paclet:Wolfram/QuantumFramework/guide/WolframQuantumComputationFramework"},
  "RefLinkPlain",
  BaseStyle->{
   "InlineFormula"}]], \
